SUMMARY:Ergodic theorems for the frontier of branching Brownian motion
DESCRIPTION:We present a short argument for the ergodic theorem of the frontier of branching Brownian motion (BBM). Our approach relies on two main observations: pairs of extremal particles observed at well-separated times must have branched early\, and pairs of early-branching extremal particles have negatively correlated positions. We will show how this yields the ergodic theorem for BBM and extends it to a \nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/16900/
